1
00:00:01,085 --> 00:00:02,086
[theme song playing]

2
00:00:02,169 --> 00:00:04,422
♪ You, just us ♪

3
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:07,967
♪ Just this, just 'cause ♪

4
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:09,677
♪ Just because ♪

5
00:00:10,678 --> 00:00:13,723
♪ When you say my name
It hits different ♪

6
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:17,768
♪ Just because ♪

7
00:00:17,852 --> 00:00:23,190
♪ Every little second feels infinite ♪

8
00:00:23,274 --> 00:00:25,067
♪ No lie, no reason ♪

9
00:00:26,444 --> 00:00:28,446
♪ No fair design ♪

10
00:00:31,073 --> 00:00:34,326
♪ I'm yours ♪

11
00:00:34,410 --> 00:00:37,121
♪ Just because ♪

12
00:00:37,204 --> 00:00:39,915
♪ Mm, just because ♪

13
00:00:42,042 --> 00:00:42,960
This drama is a work of fiction.

14
00:00:43,043 --> 00:00:44,253
The characters, events,
place names, organizations,

15
00:00:44,336 --> 00:00:45,671
and other elements depicted
are unrelated to reality.

16
00:00:45,755 --> 00:00:46,964
Some images and audio were created
using generative AI technology.

17
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,091
[Eun-ha] Are you all right?

18
00:00:49,175 --> 00:00:50,468
I'm fine.

19
00:00:52,887 --> 00:00:54,680
-[sighs]
-[Eun-ha] Oh, goodness.

20
00:01:09,862 --> 00:01:11,864
[melancholy music playing]

21
00:01:17,536 --> 00:01:19,538
[sobbing]

22
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:32,343
[clattering in distance]

23
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:36,514
[toilet flushes]

24
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:38,766
[continues sobbing]

25
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:03,290
[Eun-ha sighs]

26
00:02:03,374 --> 00:02:04,917
Should I go in?

27
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:08,838
How do I handle this?

28
00:02:08,921 --> 00:02:10,965
I've never comforted my boss before.

29
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:12,633
[footsteps approaching]

30
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:15,094
EPISODE 2

31
00:02:18,013 --> 00:02:20,432
Thank you for that.
I'll pay the cleaning bill.

32
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:24,436
Eun-ha, contact Public Relations
and I'll issue a statement.

33
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:27,064
I need to find whoever posted the video
and what their goal is.

34
00:02:27,147 --> 00:02:28,816
It must have been the car owner, right?

35
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:30,901
I went there unannounced,
so it would have been difficult

36
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:32,570
to plant someone there in advance.

37
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:35,114
More importantly,
he didn't want things to escalate,

38
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:37,783
so he doesn't have much
of a motive to do this.

39
00:02:37,867 --> 00:02:40,995
Ms. Kang,
since the camera's focused on you,

40
00:02:41,078 --> 00:02:42,621
it looks like someone
followed and filmed you.

41
00:02:42,705 --> 00:02:44,790
They used a guest ID
and posted this one video.

42
00:02:44,874 --> 00:02:46,792
I have a friend
who can trace things like this.

43
00:02:46,876 --> 00:02:48,544
I can look into it for you.

44
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:49,837
Thank you.

45
00:02:51,714 --> 00:02:53,257
[Sun-woo] Are you sure she's not AI?

46
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:54,466
Stop it!

47
00:02:57,761 --> 00:02:59,638
-[woman 1] Seriously?
-[man 1] Wow, so cool.

48
00:02:59,722 --> 00:03:00,848
[Dong-seok] Thank you.

49
00:03:00,931 --> 00:03:02,975
-[woman 2] Booked a wedding venue?
-Of course.

50
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:04,852
-[man 1] Wow. Already?
-[woman 2] When is it?

51
00:03:04,935 --> 00:03:06,145
I'll send you the invitation.

52
00:03:06,228 --> 00:03:07,438
-Of course.
-You all have to come.

53
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:09,940
-[woman 1] I'll definitely go.
-[Gi-pumm] Sincere congratulations.

54
00:03:10,024 --> 00:03:11,775
[woman 1] I'll be there no matter what.

55
00:03:12,651 --> 00:03:13,652
[Gi-pumm] Oh!

56
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:18,324
I was inconsiderate.
I want to apologize properly.

57
00:03:18,407 --> 00:03:20,367
I thought I made myself clear.

58
00:03:20,451 --> 00:03:21,660
Don't you understand?

59
00:03:22,494 --> 00:03:23,579
[chuckles softly]

60
00:03:23,662 --> 00:03:25,372
[pensive music playing]

61
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:30,210
Kang Yi-ji, do you think
you have another option besides me?

62
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:32,880
Everyone at work knows about us.

63
00:03:32,963 --> 00:03:35,799
If we end our office romance,
who do you think loses?

64
00:03:35,883 --> 00:03:36,926
Really?

65
00:03:40,387 --> 00:03:42,389
Let me make this clear.

66
00:03:42,473 --> 00:03:45,184
Mr. Kim Dong-seok and I
have already broken up.

67
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:52,566
[Gi-pumm] Well, go... go back to work.

68
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:54,109
Yeah, let's get back to work.

69
00:03:55,069 --> 00:03:56,612
I'm going to the bathroom.

70
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:58,906
Hmm.

71
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:04,328
[pensive music fades]

72
00:04:05,454 --> 00:04:06,872
[cell phone ringing]

73
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:12,044
[turnstile beeps]

74
00:04:21,095 --> 00:04:22,930
[gentle music playing]

75
00:04:33,107 --> 00:04:34,149
[door beeps]

76
00:05:00,968 --> 00:05:02,094
[sighs wearily]

77
00:05:06,265 --> 00:05:08,058
Do I seem okay right now?

78
00:05:09,059 --> 00:05:11,520
[female AI voice]
Your condition is within normal range.

79
00:05:11,603 --> 00:05:14,982
You are at a phase where your emotions
are temporarily fluctuating.

80
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:16,817
Give us a refund!

81
00:05:20,154 --> 00:05:21,321
[Yi-ji sighs softly]

82
00:05:21,405 --> 00:05:23,407
Today was really hard on me.

83
00:05:23,991 --> 00:05:27,202
Considering the circumstances,
that's perfectly understandable.

84
00:05:27,286 --> 00:05:28,579
You held up well.

85
00:05:38,672 --> 00:05:42,092
[Kyung-shim] Trust your mom
and keep seeing him this time. Okay?

86
00:05:43,510 --> 00:05:46,346
Kang Yi-ji, do you think
you have another option besides me?

87
00:05:46,430 --> 00:05:47,723
Look, just face reality.

88
00:05:47,806 --> 00:05:49,558
For you, someone like me
is the best choice.

89
00:05:51,226 --> 00:05:54,354
Will I ever be able to be with someone?

90
00:05:55,105 --> 00:05:57,483
[female AI voice]
Being alone doesn't mean being isolated.

91
00:05:57,566 --> 00:05:59,526
It means you're capable
of handling your own life.

92
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:03,405
Could I ever... love someone

93
00:06:03,489 --> 00:06:05,908
and spend the rest of my life with them?

94
00:06:06,575 --> 00:06:09,787
It's possible, but it's not something
that can be guaranteed.

95
00:06:11,205 --> 00:06:13,123
[chuckles softly]

96
00:06:13,207 --> 00:06:14,792
See that?

97
00:06:14,875 --> 00:06:17,002
Even a machine can't guarantee it.

98
00:06:19,296 --> 00:06:20,339
[chuckles wryly]

99
00:06:24,301 --> 00:06:25,552
[people chattering]

100
00:06:30,182 --> 00:06:33,393
Why are you glaring at it like that?
You got something against coffee?

101
00:06:34,895 --> 00:06:36,021
I do.

102
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:39,024
Can't drink it.
It reminds me of something.

103
00:06:39,983 --> 00:06:41,735
Ah! Tastes good.

104
00:06:44,029 --> 00:06:46,156
-Hey, guess who I ran into at work?
-Oh, who?

105
00:06:46,782 --> 00:06:48,575
Im Eun-ha. Your Milky Way.

106
00:06:48,659 --> 00:06:50,536
She works there now. [grunts]

107
00:06:52,204 --> 00:06:55,582
In high school, you two vanished
in the middle of eating tteokbokki.

108
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:59,169
It wasn't tteokbokki. It was dakgalbi.

109
00:06:59,253 --> 00:07:01,797
I was helping her find her phone. [sighs]

110
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,215
Wow, look at that memory.

111
00:07:03,298 --> 00:07:05,259
I knew it.
I'm gonna get you your first love.

112
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:07,177
[Sun-woo grunts]

113
00:07:08,595 --> 00:07:09,805
[Tae-jun scoffs]

114
00:07:09,888 --> 00:07:11,098
First love?

115
00:07:13,100 --> 00:07:14,476
Forget it.

116
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:15,727
Why would you?

117
00:07:17,104 --> 00:07:18,480
Why? Just trust me.

118
00:07:19,189 --> 00:07:21,191
I'll turn you two into Romeo and Juliet.

119
00:07:21,817 --> 00:07:24,528
Hey, uh... bro, both of them die.

120
00:07:25,696 --> 00:07:26,780
Oh, right.

121
00:07:27,698 --> 00:07:29,032
[grunts]

122
00:07:29,116 --> 00:07:31,493
-Hey, you did that on purpose, didn't you?
-[laughs]

123
00:07:31,577 --> 00:07:33,120
-Ah, you got punked.
-Ah!

124
00:07:33,203 --> 00:07:35,914
[pleasant music playing]

125
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:45,465
[turnstile beeping]

126
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:52,264
[sighs]

127
00:07:55,809 --> 00:07:56,977
LEGAL AFFAIRS SENIOR MANAGER
KANG YI-JI

128
00:07:57,060 --> 00:07:58,103
[cell phone vibrating]

129
00:07:59,521 --> 00:08:00,772
MOM

130
00:08:00,856 --> 00:08:02,441
[phone continues vibrating]

131
00:08:02,524 --> 00:08:03,525
[sighs]

132
00:08:04,776 --> 00:08:06,320
Mom, I'm busy now.

133
00:08:06,403 --> 00:08:08,614
[Kyung-shim]
I'm standing in your company's lobby.

134
00:08:08,697 --> 00:08:10,824
Come down. If you don't, I'll come up.

135
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,243
I'll be right there.

136
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:15,245
[turnstile beeps]

137
00:08:23,503 --> 00:08:24,546
Mom!

138
00:08:31,345 --> 00:08:35,891
In the ten years you've worked here,
have I ever come to see you even once?

139
00:08:36,558 --> 00:08:37,476
Mom--

140
00:08:37,559 --> 00:08:39,436
Did you really have
to make me come all this way?

141
00:08:40,312 --> 00:08:42,898
[chuckles softly]
All right, so why did you?

142
00:08:42,981 --> 00:08:45,692
You told Dong-seok you wanted to break up?

143
00:08:48,070 --> 00:08:50,072
-Yes, we broke up.
-Why?

144
00:08:52,491 --> 00:08:54,076
Let's talk outside.

145
00:08:57,204 --> 00:08:58,121
Explain this.

146
00:08:58,997 --> 00:09:00,123
I don't like that man.

147
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:03,001
[scoffs] Unbelievable.

148
00:09:03,085 --> 00:09:06,255
Do you date somebody
you don't like for three months?

149
00:09:06,838 --> 00:09:08,840
He called you every day
to ask how you were

150
00:09:08,924 --> 00:09:10,300
and you kept pushing me to see him, Mom.

151
00:09:10,384 --> 00:09:12,344
You dated him because of me?

152
00:09:12,928 --> 00:09:15,806
I kept seeing him,
but we weren't compatible. Even if we--

153
00:09:15,889 --> 00:09:17,766
Where would you find a guy like that?

154
00:09:17,849 --> 00:09:21,061
He has a respectable job, hardworking,
and he wanted you.

155
00:09:21,144 --> 00:09:23,897
You know better than anyone
that's not everything.

156
00:09:23,981 --> 00:09:26,191
I'm doing this because I know you so well.

157
00:09:26,275 --> 00:09:29,987
A guy like Dong-seok would never have
left you if you chose to be with him.

158
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:31,697
Then you'd never end up alone like me.

159
00:09:32,781 --> 00:09:34,241
-Mom--
-Enough!

160
00:09:34,324 --> 00:09:37,536
Go back inside.
You have to reconsider, no matter what.

161
00:09:37,619 --> 00:09:40,831
As far as I'm concerned,
I didn't hear anything today.

162
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:42,541
Mom, I...

163
00:09:45,002 --> 00:09:46,420
[sighs in exasperation]

164
00:09:49,840 --> 00:09:51,758
[intriguing music playing]

165
00:09:59,850 --> 00:10:02,311
You posted that hospital
threat video, didn't you?

166
00:10:02,978 --> 00:10:05,939
[sighs] Come on. I'd be crazy
to stir up drama like that.

167
00:10:06,023 --> 00:10:07,232
I'm asking if you pulled that stunt

168
00:10:07,316 --> 00:10:09,651
'cause you didn't have the confidence
to compete with her properly.

169
00:10:09,735 --> 00:10:12,738
If Ms. Kang gets pushed out now,
who benefits the most? It's you.

170
00:10:12,821 --> 00:10:14,531
I swear it wasn't me.

171
00:10:15,949 --> 00:10:18,910
Does Kang Yi-ji
use her head for decoration? Huh?

172
00:10:18,994 --> 00:10:20,454
She always goes on about principles.

173
00:10:20,537 --> 00:10:22,831
Who do you think she pissed off
to cause this?

174
00:10:23,707 --> 00:10:27,419
Wow! This video of her getting
splashed with coffee is blowing up.

175
00:10:27,502 --> 00:10:28,712
[laughs]

176
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:32,841
"Chronic Motors employee
Ms. Kang threatens car owner."

177
00:10:35,594 --> 00:10:36,928
Have the video taken down.

178
00:10:37,012 --> 00:10:38,847
It's okay as long as
it doesn't get any bigger.

179
00:10:38,930 --> 00:10:41,224
Hey, wait a sec. What if this reaches HQ?

180
00:10:41,975 --> 00:10:44,936
[sighs] Then it might not just end
with Kang Yi-ji's career.

181
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:55,989
Frankly, there's only one person
who would have a grudge against Ms. Kang.

182
00:10:56,573 --> 00:10:57,657
Who?

183
00:10:58,241 --> 00:10:59,618
[whispers] Mr. Jung Ki-tae.

184
00:11:00,202 --> 00:11:01,119
[woman] Really?

185
00:11:01,828 --> 00:11:04,956
How did our Ms. Kang
get dragged into something like this?

186
00:11:05,916 --> 00:11:08,418
But don't you find her
a little suffocating,

187
00:11:08,502 --> 00:11:10,337
since she never lets anything slide?

188
00:11:10,420 --> 00:11:11,880
Why are you being like this, hmm?

189
00:11:12,464 --> 00:11:15,133
You got told off for lacking competence.
You say she's too demanding.

190
00:11:15,217 --> 00:11:18,303
The one who's good at her job
ends up being called ruthless. Hmm?

191
00:11:18,887 --> 00:11:22,808
I hear Legal Affairs is having
a team dinner tonight. [chuckles]

192
00:11:22,891 --> 00:11:24,434
Why are you interested
in our team's dinner?

193
00:11:24,518 --> 00:11:26,395
Legal Affairs and the Secretary's Office

194
00:11:26,478 --> 00:11:29,231
are supposed to be partners
in keeping confidentiality.

195
00:11:30,690 --> 00:11:33,193
You know,
the CEO's office and Legal Affairs

196
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:34,736
are right next to each other.

197
00:11:34,820 --> 00:11:36,696
Please, let me join your dinner, too.

198
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:39,950
I really want to feel like I belong here.
Can't you bring me in?

199
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:42,160
Then come and make yourself useful
grilling the meat.

200
00:11:42,244 --> 00:11:43,078
[Ga-heun groans]

201
00:11:44,746 --> 00:11:46,873
By the way, do you know
where Mr. Han Sun-woo is?

202
00:11:46,957 --> 00:11:48,959
[playful music playing]

203
00:11:51,962 --> 00:11:53,672
Let's cross check
the statement we're sending

204
00:11:53,755 --> 00:11:56,091
-to the Public Relations Team.
-Hmm.

205
00:11:56,174 --> 00:11:57,717
This...

206
00:11:58,468 --> 00:12:01,096
Mr. Han, we're having
a welcome dinner for you today.

207
00:12:01,179 --> 00:12:02,848
Nobody mentioned that.

208
00:12:02,931 --> 00:12:05,058
Is it a dinner
for the whole Legal Affairs team?

209
00:12:05,142 --> 00:12:08,437
Mr. Jung Ki-tae especially booked
the galbi place out front.

210
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,397
I heard the meat there is really good.

211
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,315
I can just ask Ms. Kang first.

212
00:12:12,399 --> 00:12:14,860
She has too much on her plate
to think about that now.

213
00:12:16,153 --> 00:12:18,321
Just come.
I'm really good at grilling meat.

214
00:12:19,156 --> 00:12:20,615
If Ms. Kang isn't going,

215
00:12:20,699 --> 00:12:22,492
-then I don't think we need to--
-Stop!

216
00:12:22,576 --> 00:12:26,580
[sighs wearily]
This is good for the company. Okay?

217
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:27,581
Yeah.

218
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,375
See you later.

219
00:12:35,422 --> 00:12:36,882
[scoffs]

220
00:12:38,758 --> 00:12:41,970
CHRONIC MOTORS, A COMPANY THAT
ABUSES POWER, USING FAMILY TO MAKE THREATS

221
00:12:46,766 --> 00:12:47,726
[knock on door]

222
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:51,521
[door closes]

223
00:12:54,149 --> 00:12:55,484
[Byung-je sighs]

224
00:12:55,567 --> 00:12:59,571
Hello, sir. I'm finalizing the official
statement with the Public Relations Team.

225
00:12:59,654 --> 00:13:01,698
We'll send out the press release
by the end of today.

226
00:13:01,781 --> 00:13:02,782
Never mind that.

227
00:13:02,866 --> 00:13:04,493
What I want to know right now...

228
00:13:04,576 --> 00:13:05,952
COUNTRY HEAD, KOREA
SONG BYUNG-JE

229
00:13:06,036 --> 00:13:08,371
...is what you think about this incident.

230
00:13:08,455 --> 00:13:10,248
My thoughts are the same.

231
00:13:10,332 --> 00:13:11,917
I did meet with the car owner,

232
00:13:12,501 --> 00:13:15,879
but I absolutely did not
threaten him over his family issue.

233
00:13:15,962 --> 00:13:19,174
I believe you, but the problem is
the other people don't.

234
00:13:20,592 --> 00:13:24,304
But... how did someone on the outside know

235
00:13:24,387 --> 00:13:27,724
when just the two of you
were meeting and filmed it?

236
00:13:27,807 --> 00:13:30,227
Honestly, I don't know that either.

237
00:13:30,310 --> 00:13:32,145
If you don't, then who does?

238
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:36,900
In fact, you handled this case by yourself
from beginning to end, didn't you?

239
00:13:36,983 --> 00:13:40,278
Besides, suddenly visiting the hospital
two days before the meeting

240
00:13:40,362 --> 00:13:42,864
was done completely on your own volition.

241
00:13:44,115 --> 00:13:45,450
Think about it, sir.

242
00:13:45,534 --> 00:13:46,743
The one who got hit with coffee

243
00:13:46,826 --> 00:13:48,828
and the one who was verbally abused,
that was all me.

244
00:13:48,912 --> 00:13:51,915
But even so, there still hasn't been
any action taken by the company.

245
00:13:51,998 --> 00:13:53,750
[Byung-je] This has escalated too much!

246
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:57,629
From the company's position,
how can we entrust external duties to you

247
00:13:57,712 --> 00:14:00,173
when you've damaged our image this badly?

248
00:14:00,257 --> 00:14:02,259
[pensive music playing]

249
00:14:03,051 --> 00:14:06,012
Well, sir, are you saying that...

250
00:14:06,096 --> 00:14:08,932
The PR Team says
the statement has been revised.

251
00:14:09,015 --> 00:14:11,268
-Please take a look.
-You look at it.

252
00:14:11,351 --> 00:14:15,522
Yes. Well, it says there were no threats
and offer us apologies,

253
00:14:15,605 --> 00:14:16,982
but the last line is key.

254
00:14:17,065 --> 00:14:21,403
"To maintain our organization's stability
and prevent additional controversy,

255
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:23,655
we at Chronic Motors promise that...

256
00:14:25,907 --> 00:14:28,827
effective tomorrow, the employee concerned

257
00:14:28,910 --> 00:14:31,121
will be transferred out of Legal Affairs."

258
00:14:39,713 --> 00:14:41,047
[Yi-ji gasps softly]

259
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:44,551
Sir, you know very well
that I've worked for this company

260
00:14:44,634 --> 00:14:46,261
for the past ten years without issues.

261
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:49,472
Look, Ms. Kang,
this incident even reached headquarters,

262
00:14:49,556 --> 00:14:51,808
and the situation was really bad for you.

263
00:14:51,891 --> 00:14:54,144
If Mr. Song hadn't decided
to cover for you--

264
00:14:54,227 --> 00:14:56,605
Mr. Jung, please step outside.

265
00:15:00,317 --> 00:15:01,776
[pensive music fades]

266
00:15:02,694 --> 00:15:05,071
[door opens, closes]

267
00:15:06,906 --> 00:15:08,491
This is the company's decision.

268
00:15:08,575 --> 00:15:11,786
Report to the
Management Support Team tomorrow.

269
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:14,748
For now, a department transfer
is the best option.

270
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:22,172
It seems...
you've already made up your mind.

271
00:15:22,255 --> 00:15:24,299
Go home and get some rest for today.

272
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:30,889
[Yi-ji] Understood, sir.

273
00:15:31,806 --> 00:15:34,726
[sighs] There are two hours left
before the work day ends.

274
00:15:34,809 --> 00:15:37,520
I'll finish the tasks I was doing
in Legal Affairs before going home.

275
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,900
[Byung-je] Kang Yi-ji.

276
00:15:42,734 --> 00:15:45,862
You're good at your job. That's for sure.

277
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:49,199
I also had high expectations of you.

278
00:15:50,575 --> 00:15:54,079
However, an organization is not a place
that runs on principles alone.

279
00:15:54,162 --> 00:15:55,747
It holds on through relationships.

280
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:59,125
Someone as strong as you
is bound to break someday.

281
00:16:00,669 --> 00:16:02,879
You should just make
a graceful exit instead.

282
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:05,173
Even if you go down
to Management Support now,

283
00:16:05,256 --> 00:16:06,841
there won't be a desk for you.

284
00:16:06,925 --> 00:16:08,968
It's impressive you've lasted this long.

285
00:16:17,811 --> 00:16:19,938
[poignant music playing]

286
00:16:21,398 --> 00:16:22,691
[door opens]

287
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:32,784
[Ga-heun]
The atmosphere right now is no joke.

288
00:16:32,867 --> 00:16:34,494
[cell phones vibrate and ding]

289
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:39,749
[Do-a] The rumors about
the personnel transfer are true.

290
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:42,043
[Gi-pumm]
Ms. Kang, who's so good at her job?

291
00:16:58,768 --> 00:17:00,437
[poignant music fades]

292
00:17:02,647 --> 00:17:04,274
-[knock on door]
-Yes.

293
00:17:04,816 --> 00:17:05,817
[door opens]

294
00:17:08,737 --> 00:17:09,863
[door closes]

295
00:17:09,946 --> 00:17:11,281
Ms. Kang...

296
00:17:11,906 --> 00:17:14,534
You need to clear everything out
by tomorrow morning.

297
00:17:14,617 --> 00:17:16,077
It's the CEO's orders.

298
00:17:16,161 --> 00:17:17,954
You can leave that there.

299
00:17:26,838 --> 00:17:28,256
CHRONIC MOTORS LEGAL AFFAIRS

300
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:29,966
LEAVE CHAT

301
00:17:30,049 --> 00:17:32,385
DO YOU WANT TO LEAVE THE TEAM CHAT?
LEAVE

302
00:17:35,138 --> 00:17:36,264
[sighs deeply]

303
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:38,892
[knock on door]

304
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:40,602
-Yes.
-[door opens]

305
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,815
Ms. Kang, about that guy
who put up the video,

306
00:17:45,899 --> 00:17:49,444
they posted on a message board
about a month ago using the same ID.

307
00:17:49,527 --> 00:17:52,113
They asked about location tracking apps
for his wife's phone.

308
00:17:52,197 --> 00:17:53,907
I'm no longer on the Legal Affairs Team.

309
00:17:54,365 --> 00:17:56,868
You don't have to report to me
about that incident.

310
00:17:57,744 --> 00:17:59,496
But you're the victim here.

311
00:18:01,915 --> 00:18:06,211
I'm sure the harm I suffered is nothing
compared to the company's losses.

312
00:18:12,884 --> 00:18:14,052
Would you mind leaving?

313
00:18:23,019 --> 00:18:24,229
[door opens]

314
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:29,442
[door closes]

315
00:18:31,986 --> 00:18:33,988
[pensive music playing]

316
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:14,779
[tempo rises]

317
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:37,802
[light switch clicks]

318
00:19:45,894 --> 00:19:46,895
You startled me.

319
00:19:46,978 --> 00:19:48,938
Why are you still here?

320
00:19:49,022 --> 00:19:51,024
Didn't you say there was
a welcome dinner for you today?

321
00:19:51,107 --> 00:19:52,817
I made an excuse and didn't go.

322
00:19:52,901 --> 00:19:54,402
The guest of honor didn't go?

323
00:19:54,485 --> 00:19:57,655
[scoffs] Do you want
to get on their bad side already?

324
00:19:57,739 --> 00:20:01,200
[sighs] I didn't know any better
because I'm still new.

325
00:20:02,285 --> 00:20:04,287
Couldn't you just give me
a welcome dinner instead?

326
00:20:05,121 --> 00:20:09,667
Hmm. I'm sorry,
but you're an assistant to Legal Affairs.

327
00:20:10,376 --> 00:20:13,004
I am not part of the team anymore now.

328
00:20:13,087 --> 00:20:15,715
You're going
to the Management Support Team tomorrow.

329
00:20:16,424 --> 00:20:20,011
Today isn't over yet,
so aren't you still with Legal Affairs?

330
00:20:22,555 --> 00:20:24,015
That's true, actually.

331
00:20:25,433 --> 00:20:27,477
However, I'll decide on the menu.

332
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,020
DEOKWON FIRE JJAMPPONG

333
00:20:29,103 --> 00:20:31,022
LIFE IS SPICY! ENDURE IT
WITH EVEN SPICIER FIRE JJAMPPONG!

334
00:20:31,105 --> 00:20:34,108
[romantic music playing]

335
00:20:40,114 --> 00:20:41,366
FINISHING YOUR JJAMPPONG
STRICTLY FORBIDDEN

336
00:20:41,449 --> 00:20:43,034
ONLY EAT AS MUCH AS YOU CAN HANDLE

337
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,336
[sighs]

338
00:20:53,419 --> 00:20:54,295
-[Yi-ji] Excuse me, sir.
-Yes?

339
00:20:54,379 --> 00:20:55,755
One level four and...

340
00:20:56,255 --> 00:20:58,925
Oh, since this is your first time,
level one would be better for you.

341
00:20:59,008 --> 00:21:01,135
[laughs] Oh, of course not.

342
00:21:01,219 --> 00:21:03,388
Sir, please give us two at level four.

343
00:21:03,471 --> 00:21:05,390
[owner] Two more level fours.

344
00:21:06,349 --> 00:21:07,976
[romantic music continues]

345
00:21:14,399 --> 00:21:15,733
[blowing]

346
00:21:20,947 --> 00:21:22,532
[slurping]

347
00:21:23,074 --> 00:21:23,992
[sniffs]

348
00:21:24,784 --> 00:21:26,077
[slurping]

349
00:21:30,832 --> 00:21:31,833
[exhales]

350
00:21:34,377 --> 00:21:35,837
[Sun-woo clears throat]

351
00:21:37,547 --> 00:21:39,382
[slurping]

352
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,134
[coughing]

353
00:21:42,969 --> 00:21:43,970
Are you all right?

354
00:21:44,554 --> 00:21:47,348
-Didn't you say you liked spicy food?
-[coughing]

355
00:21:47,932 --> 00:21:48,808
[Sun-woo] Oh!

356
00:21:48,891 --> 00:21:51,352
Oh, can you...
can you open this for me, please?

357
00:21:51,436 --> 00:21:52,729
[coughs]

358
00:21:54,772 --> 00:21:56,524
-I can't open it.
-Open it quick!

359
00:21:59,902 --> 00:22:01,863
-Here, drink this.
-Okay. Thank you.

360
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:11,164
[exhales in relief] Ah!

361
00:22:11,247 --> 00:22:12,415
[laughing]

362
00:22:13,082 --> 00:22:15,376
-[Eun-ha] One level four here, please!
-[owner] Got it.

363
00:22:15,460 --> 00:22:16,544
[Yi-ji] How come you're here?

364
00:22:16,627 --> 00:22:18,921
-Is the team dinner already over?
-No, I escaped.

365
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:21,049
Sun-woo told me you two were here.

366
00:22:22,091 --> 00:22:24,427
I was told headquarters
never even brought you up.

367
00:22:25,303 --> 00:22:27,263
Probably the CEO and Mr. Jung.

368
00:22:27,346 --> 00:22:28,973
You think I didn't know that?

369
00:22:30,183 --> 00:22:33,978
All right. From now on, you two should
flatter people a little when you need to.

370
00:22:34,062 --> 00:22:36,022
And at crucial moments,
step over me and go ahead.

371
00:22:36,105 --> 00:22:37,690
I'll be just fine.

372
00:22:39,484 --> 00:22:41,611
Ms. Kang,
if there's any way I can help you

373
00:22:41,694 --> 00:22:43,905
with the Management Support Team,
let me know.

374
00:22:43,988 --> 00:22:47,992
Yeah, and I'll make sure
I find out whoever posted that video.

375
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,871
-Thank you.
-Yeah. [sighs]

376
00:22:51,954 --> 00:22:53,998
You get used to it in time
if you eat it a lot.

377
00:22:54,082 --> 00:22:55,333
A lot? [hiccups]

378
00:22:56,084 --> 00:22:57,001
What, this?!

379
00:22:58,586 --> 00:23:00,129
[both laughing]

380
00:23:00,213 --> 00:23:01,589
[train rattling]

381
00:23:01,672 --> 00:23:02,840
[soft music playing]

382
00:23:02,924 --> 00:23:05,259
-Thank you so much for the ride.
-Thank you.

383
00:23:05,843 --> 00:23:07,095
It's okay. It was on my way.

384
00:23:07,804 --> 00:23:11,140
I'm so upset that I won't be seeing you
anymore starting tomorrow.

385
00:23:11,224 --> 00:23:12,892
[chuckles]

386
00:23:12,975 --> 00:23:15,269
Anyone listening
would think I was going to HQ in Europe.

387
00:23:16,813 --> 00:23:18,648
I don't know if it's my place to say this,

388
00:23:18,731 --> 00:23:22,610
but someone like you would have
plenty of people wanting to scout you.

389
00:23:22,693 --> 00:23:24,112
What about another company?

390
00:23:26,614 --> 00:23:28,407
When I first joined the company,

391
00:23:28,491 --> 00:23:31,786
I remember over 80%
of the employees were men.

392
00:23:32,328 --> 00:23:36,541
Everyone asked what I could
possibly even accomplish there.

393
00:23:38,251 --> 00:23:39,877
So I held on even more intensely.

394
00:23:39,961 --> 00:23:42,713
During those ten years,
I never ran away once.

395
00:23:44,257 --> 00:23:46,425
If I give up now, it would feel like

396
00:23:46,509 --> 00:23:48,845
the past ten years of my life
were for nothing.

397
00:23:48,928 --> 00:23:51,389
I have to get back up right where I fell.

398
00:23:56,102 --> 00:23:58,938
Listening to you now,
I can say for sure you're not AI.

399
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:02,900
Hey! What'd you say? [laughs]

400
00:24:04,443 --> 00:24:06,320
[soft music fades]

401
00:24:11,742 --> 00:24:13,452
[Sun-woo]
Are you sure you'll be all right?

402
00:24:13,536 --> 00:24:16,122
When I looked at the comments, even
your personal info was getting spread.

403
00:24:16,205 --> 00:24:18,499
Wouldn't it maybe be better
to stay at your mother's for a while?

404
00:24:19,375 --> 00:24:22,712
Wouldn't it be more serious
if my mother's address got out?

405
00:24:22,795 --> 00:24:24,881
Those people only
hurl abusive words online.

406
00:24:24,964 --> 00:24:26,340
They won't do anything in real life.

407
00:24:26,424 --> 00:24:27,800
I'm fine. Don't worry.

408
00:24:27,884 --> 00:24:29,093
Get home safe.

409
00:24:44,859 --> 00:24:46,485
[wistful music playing]

410
00:24:49,614 --> 00:24:52,700
This is Kang Yi-ji,
who just joined Legal Affairs.

411
00:24:52,783 --> 00:24:53,743
Applause!

412
00:24:55,703 --> 00:24:58,414
Nice to meet you.
Let's work well together. [chuckles]

413
00:24:59,957 --> 00:25:02,627
-Manager Kang. Congratulations.
-Thank you.

414
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:04,795
-[co-workers congratulating]
-Thank you.

415
00:25:04,879 --> 00:25:06,297
Good job, Manager Kang!

416
00:25:06,380 --> 00:25:08,049
[Byung-je laughs]

417
00:25:08,132 --> 00:25:10,509
[wistful music continues]

418
00:25:39,830 --> 00:25:42,041
[wistful music fades]

419
00:25:42,124 --> 00:25:45,336
How could they transfer her
to another department overnight?

420
00:25:45,419 --> 00:25:50,049
She spent ten years in Legal Affairs,
and suddenly, Management Support?

421
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:52,343
[Sun-woo sighs]

422
00:25:53,552 --> 00:25:57,306
By the way, why did you get off here?
This is the way to my place.

423
00:25:57,390 --> 00:25:58,724
[playful music playing]

424
00:25:58,808 --> 00:26:01,269
Didn't you say you were moving tomorrow?
I'm here to help.

425
00:26:01,352 --> 00:26:03,396
Oh... kay.

426
00:26:05,982 --> 00:26:07,608
Does Tae-jun still draw comics?

427
00:26:07,692 --> 00:26:10,152
I've been waiting so eagerly
for him to start a series.

428
00:26:10,236 --> 00:26:12,321
I should tell him he's got a fan
waiting for it, you know.

429
00:26:12,405 --> 00:26:14,490
Hey, should I ask him to come join us?

430
00:26:15,825 --> 00:26:16,826
Huh!

431
00:26:20,871 --> 00:26:22,164
[tires squealing]

432
00:26:24,917 --> 00:26:27,837
[ominous music playing]

433
00:26:43,978 --> 00:26:45,896
[ominous music builds]

434
00:26:51,694 --> 00:26:54,572
WONDERING WHERE TO SELL YOUR USED CAR?
WE GUARANTEE THE HIGHEST PRICE!

435
00:26:55,197 --> 00:26:57,325
[flyers rustling]

436
00:26:58,784 --> 00:26:59,910
[exhales in relief]

437
00:27:01,329 --> 00:27:03,331
[pensive music playing]

438
00:27:06,083 --> 00:27:07,376
[cell phone keypad tones]

439
00:27:08,669 --> 00:27:10,629
[line ringing]

440
00:27:11,547 --> 00:27:12,965
Yeah.

441
00:27:13,049 --> 00:27:14,800
Can I come over right now?

442
00:27:18,054 --> 00:27:19,221
[Sun-woo] Tae-jun.

443
00:27:19,305 --> 00:27:20,806
Oh, you're back.

444
00:27:20,890 --> 00:27:22,058
I can't get this right.

445
00:27:26,562 --> 00:27:29,315
[soft music playing]

446
00:27:31,442 --> 00:27:33,027
[Eun-ha chuckles]

447
00:27:33,110 --> 00:27:34,278
[Eun-ha] Hi!

448
00:27:34,862 --> 00:27:36,655
-[playful music playing]
-[nervously] Um... [sniffs]

449
00:27:39,825 --> 00:27:41,202
It's been a while.

450
00:27:41,911 --> 00:27:45,373
Has it been six years? The last time
was before you went to the military.

451
00:27:45,456 --> 00:27:49,919
No, three years... and two months?
I did see you at your graduation.

452
00:27:51,045 --> 00:27:52,797
You... you came then?

453
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,382
Uh...

454
00:27:55,925 --> 00:27:57,009
[chuckles sheepishly]

455
00:27:58,219 --> 00:27:59,345
Um...

456
00:28:01,305 --> 00:28:02,807
Im Eun-ha...

457
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:04,350
how have you been?

458
00:28:04,433 --> 00:28:05,893
[Sun-woo snorts, chuckles]

459
00:28:06,936 --> 00:28:10,606
Mm. Jung Tae-jun.
I never thought we'd meet again like this.

460
00:28:15,236 --> 00:28:16,112
Ah!

461
00:28:16,654 --> 00:28:19,115
Hey, I already told you.
She's my mentor at work.

462
00:28:19,198 --> 00:28:21,242
When I said I was moving,
she wanted to help.

463
00:28:21,325 --> 00:28:23,911
What are you saying?
I just came to see the school!

464
00:28:25,204 --> 00:28:26,497
Or basketball.

465
00:28:27,540 --> 00:28:28,541
No, that... that moon!

466
00:28:29,125 --> 00:28:31,460
I wanted to see the moon from here.

467
00:28:31,544 --> 00:28:33,170
Ah! Moon-watching.

468
00:28:33,879 --> 00:28:35,423
Mm. Is that so?

469
00:28:35,506 --> 00:28:37,675
[inhales sharply]
Then I'll do the packing.

470
00:28:37,758 --> 00:28:39,093
You go look at the moon with Tae-jun.

471
00:28:39,176 --> 00:28:40,886
S-S-Sun-woo.

472
00:28:40,970 --> 00:28:42,388
Don't I have to pack?

473
00:28:44,473 --> 00:28:45,516
-Tae-jun.
-Yes?

474
00:28:45,599 --> 00:28:46,934
Where's that thing?

475
00:28:47,017 --> 00:28:50,813
-What?
-Knowing... when to take a hint?

476
00:28:50,896 --> 00:28:52,106
Go look at the moon!

477
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:53,983
I'm out.

478
00:28:54,984 --> 00:28:57,069
-[Eun-ha] Okay, bye.
-[Tae-jun] Go...

479
00:28:57,153 --> 00:28:58,571
[chuckles]

480
00:28:59,405 --> 00:29:01,699
[chuckles nervously] Uh...

481
00:29:03,451 --> 00:29:05,161
-[classical music playing]
-[door opens]

482
00:29:06,620 --> 00:29:07,830
I'm here.

483
00:29:08,330 --> 00:29:09,415
[door closes]

484
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:13,752
What's this?

485
00:29:15,296 --> 00:29:19,216
Today's concept
is a widow attending a banquet

486
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:23,095
hosted by a rich landowner
in an 18th century European village.

487
00:29:24,054 --> 00:29:28,100
[sighs] If I'd known, I'd have
brought wine instead of beer then.

488
00:29:28,184 --> 00:29:29,226
[soft music playing]

489
00:29:29,310 --> 00:29:31,479
I think your company's
gone a little crazy.

490
00:29:31,562 --> 00:29:35,065
Even a corner store manager
wouldn't handle things that way.

491
00:29:35,149 --> 00:29:36,859
It must have been hard.

492
00:29:36,942 --> 00:29:38,569
[sighs] When you're troubled,

493
00:29:38,652 --> 00:29:40,905
the power of love
is the best way to get through it.

494
00:29:42,573 --> 00:29:43,741
I think that I...

495
00:29:44,450 --> 00:29:48,454
[sighs] I'm not capable of sharing
my everyday life with someone, you know.

496
00:29:49,622 --> 00:29:52,082
Maybe it's because
I use up all my energy at work.

497
00:29:52,166 --> 00:29:54,835
When I come home,
I don't even have the strength to change,

498
00:29:54,919 --> 00:29:56,712
and the messages start piling up.

499
00:29:58,339 --> 00:30:01,008
I don't have the energy to respond.

500
00:30:01,091 --> 00:30:04,053
If it was work or dating,
I'd always pick work.

501
00:30:04,595 --> 00:30:07,056
As expected. A woman married to her job.

502
00:30:08,307 --> 00:30:10,351
So my brother-in-law was your work.

503
00:30:11,894 --> 00:30:12,853
Goodness.

504
00:30:14,772 --> 00:30:16,065
Oh, dear.

505
00:30:16,148 --> 00:30:17,399
[soft music fades]

506
00:30:27,201 --> 00:30:28,827
Hello, Ms. Kang.

507
00:30:31,872 --> 00:30:34,041
[woman] Oh, you're here, Ms. Kang?

508
00:30:34,124 --> 00:30:35,376
[chuckles softly]

509
00:30:36,168 --> 00:30:37,294
Good morning, Ms. Lee.

510
00:30:37,378 --> 00:30:41,382
Yeah. Oh, after ten years in your office,
you must have a lot of things.

511
00:30:42,091 --> 00:30:45,219
You weren't expecting an office, right?
We don't have those.

512
00:30:45,302 --> 00:30:47,054
Or what, should I give you my room?

513
00:30:47,638 --> 00:30:50,432
Of course not. I don't care where I work.

514
00:30:50,516 --> 00:30:52,935
-Happy to be here now with you.
-Right.

515
00:30:54,728 --> 00:30:56,981
You can't throw your weight around here
like you did before.

516
00:30:57,606 --> 00:30:59,817
Still, if you can, give it all you've got.

517
00:30:59,900 --> 00:31:00,943
Okay?

518
00:31:02,152 --> 00:31:04,071
Though your outfit today is, um...

519
00:31:06,323 --> 00:31:07,283
not bad.

520
00:31:23,966 --> 00:31:25,509
[sneezing]

521
00:31:25,593 --> 00:31:26,885
[sighs]

522
00:31:30,472 --> 00:31:32,641
[Sun-woo] You sit here. I get hot easy,

523
00:31:33,267 --> 00:31:35,394
so I prefer being
right under the air vent.

524
00:31:36,353 --> 00:31:38,564
But why would you ever have to sit here?

525
00:31:38,647 --> 00:31:41,233
I was told to go and help
the Management Support Team.

526
00:31:41,317 --> 00:31:43,152
They're sending
the Legal Affairs assistant

527
00:31:43,235 --> 00:31:44,361
to the Management Support Team?

528
00:31:44,445 --> 00:31:47,781
Yeah. They said I could apply
for a department change in my orientation,

529
00:31:47,865 --> 00:31:49,033
so I said I'd like to follow you.

530
00:31:49,617 --> 00:31:51,410
You can see I'm pretty loyal.

531
00:31:51,493 --> 00:31:55,289
I guess since everyone knows you got hired
because of the vehicle fire accident,

532
00:31:55,372 --> 00:31:58,584
they thought it'd be better
to keep you with me during your probation.

533
00:31:58,667 --> 00:32:01,629
How can you interpret
my loyalty like that?

534
00:32:01,712 --> 00:32:02,671
[cell phone vibrating]

535
00:32:06,216 --> 00:32:09,845
[Yi-ji] Thank you for your offer,
but I'm not interested for now.

536
00:32:10,638 --> 00:32:14,266
Are there...
entry level openings available?

537
00:32:14,350 --> 00:32:16,810
[woman] We don't have anything
for an entry level.

538
00:32:16,894 --> 00:32:19,146
It would be better to keep them
with you for a few years

539
00:32:19,229 --> 00:32:21,482
-and build their experience.
-I see.

540
00:32:21,565 --> 00:32:24,526
Frankly, I'm only making this offer
because it's you.

541
00:32:24,610 --> 00:32:27,363
The job market isn't welcoming
to women your age.

542
00:32:27,446 --> 00:32:29,823
Just when they're in
their prime working years,

543
00:32:29,907 --> 00:32:32,910
they leave to get married,
or take maternity leave,

544
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:34,370
and then the company has to rehire.

545
00:32:34,453 --> 00:32:35,871
Yes, I understand.

546
00:32:35,954 --> 00:32:37,373
I'll call you another time.

547
00:32:40,250 --> 00:32:41,335
[line disconnects]

548
00:32:44,046 --> 00:32:45,881
[upbeat music playing]

549
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:49,343
I'm sure you'll do fine,
but keep a close eye on Ms. Kang.

550
00:32:49,426 --> 00:32:50,302
Yes, sir.

551
00:32:50,386 --> 00:32:53,806
I hope she doesn't make even more
achievements after changing departments.

552
00:32:53,889 --> 00:32:55,849
Goodness, that won't happen.

553
00:32:55,933 --> 00:32:59,311
I'd rather have an obedient,
gentle puppy for a subordinate

554
00:32:59,395 --> 00:33:01,313
than a wild dog running around on its own.

555
00:33:02,272 --> 00:33:03,565
[scoffs] A puppy?

556
00:33:03,649 --> 00:33:04,650
Hmm.

557
00:33:04,733 --> 00:33:07,069
[all laughing]

558
00:33:08,070 --> 00:33:10,656
Kang Yi-ji could never be a puppy.

559
00:33:10,739 --> 00:33:14,034
I'll work on her properly,
and I'll tame her in time.

560
00:33:14,118 --> 00:33:17,162
-[Jung-eun laughs]
-I've always wondered one thing, though.

561
00:33:17,705 --> 00:33:20,708
Tell me, why do you dislike her so much?

562
00:33:20,791 --> 00:33:24,336
Mm. With her face and the way
she dresses, she kind of stands out.

563
00:33:24,420 --> 00:33:26,630
Gosh, I don't like
a single thing she does.

564
00:33:26,714 --> 00:33:28,298
Ah!

565
00:33:28,382 --> 00:33:31,677
You're saying you dislike her
because she has good style?

566
00:33:35,472 --> 00:33:39,101
Sometimes... when I say something judgy,

567
00:33:39,184 --> 00:33:41,353
you really do take it in a bad way.

568
00:33:42,271 --> 00:33:43,689
What?

569
00:33:43,772 --> 00:33:45,232
[suspenseful music playing]

570
00:33:46,066 --> 00:33:48,819
[Ki-tae chuckles]
It's a compliment, right?

571
00:33:48,902 --> 00:33:50,571
-[Byung-je sighs]
-[Ki-tae laughs]

572
00:33:50,654 --> 00:33:52,114
[suspenseful music fades]

573
00:33:54,450 --> 00:33:56,326
[woman] I'll be going. Good job.

574
00:33:56,410 --> 00:33:57,578
-Good work.
-[man 1] See you.

575
00:33:57,661 --> 00:33:58,746
[man 2] We can do the rest tomorrow.

576
00:33:58,829 --> 00:34:02,166
Ms. Lee asked you to organize these
within two days.

577
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:04,626
[sighs] She said it's urgent.

578
00:34:07,045 --> 00:34:09,715
Gosh, the... formats are a mess.

579
00:34:09,798 --> 00:34:11,049
Two days won't be enough.

580
00:34:11,842 --> 00:34:13,135
What?

581
00:34:13,218 --> 00:34:17,431
Is there anyone here who doesn't know
how good Ms. Kang is at her job?

582
00:34:17,514 --> 00:34:19,767
It's your first assignment on our team.

583
00:34:19,850 --> 00:34:20,934
Will it be too much?

584
00:34:22,269 --> 00:34:23,353
It's perfectly fine.

585
00:34:23,437 --> 00:34:25,147
I can finish it in two days.

586
00:34:25,981 --> 00:34:28,108
Okay. Good luck.

587
00:34:28,192 --> 00:34:29,902
[pensive music playing]

588
00:34:32,654 --> 00:34:33,614
[sighs]

589
00:34:44,374 --> 00:34:47,878
Ms. Kang, who would need
these old materials in such a hurry?

590
00:34:47,961 --> 00:34:49,296
[Yi-ji] What difference would it make?

591
00:34:50,130 --> 00:34:52,466
Take one more volume. I'll do three more.

592
00:34:53,884 --> 00:34:55,594
She's giving you a hard time on purpose.

593
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:56,804
That's why I have to be perfect.

594
00:34:56,887 --> 00:35:00,265
So she gets no pleasure
out of making things difficult.

595
00:35:01,517 --> 00:35:05,562
I can't get into a fight on the first day,
so let's just wait and see.

596
00:35:06,522 --> 00:35:08,023
[papers rustling]

597
00:35:13,070 --> 00:35:14,321
[car horn honks]

598
00:35:16,156 --> 00:35:18,700
-[Yi-ji] Want to get in?
-Ah, thank you, but I'll be fine.

599
00:35:18,784 --> 00:35:21,620
-If you're not getting in, I'll go.
-No, no! I'll get in. I'll get in.

600
00:35:24,748 --> 00:35:25,916
[car door shuts]

601
00:35:30,671 --> 00:35:31,797
[Yi-ji] Put your address in.

602
00:35:31,880 --> 00:35:33,590
Ah, thank you.

603
00:35:34,174 --> 00:35:36,969
You can drop me
somewhere around Artium Palace.

604
00:35:37,052 --> 00:35:38,303
Close it. I live there, too.

605
00:35:39,304 --> 00:35:40,389
What? Really?

606
00:35:41,974 --> 00:35:43,267
[chuckles] Oh!

607
00:35:44,101 --> 00:35:45,269
[chuckling]

608
00:35:47,729 --> 00:35:51,108
By the way... your phone is overheating.

609
00:35:51,191 --> 00:35:54,236
You must have a lot of apps
running in the background here.

610
00:35:55,654 --> 00:35:57,364
Do you play games a lot?

611
00:35:57,447 --> 00:35:59,491
[Yi-ji] Do I look like I play games?

612
00:36:01,869 --> 00:36:03,871
Oh, about that person
who posted the video.

613
00:36:03,954 --> 00:36:06,665
We're looking for them,
but they're routing through a VPN,

614
00:36:06,748 --> 00:36:08,041
so it's taking some time.

615
00:36:08,125 --> 00:36:10,002
That post that was made under the same ID

616
00:36:10,085 --> 00:36:13,463
asking about installing apps
on his wife's phone... Huh?

617
00:36:14,339 --> 00:36:16,758
Something is really eating up
your phone storage.

618
00:36:16,842 --> 00:36:18,010
Could this be hacked?

619
00:36:19,177 --> 00:36:21,221
There's no way that could be.

620
00:36:21,305 --> 00:36:24,933
This only happens when someone's
tracking someone's location, though.

621
00:36:25,017 --> 00:36:26,393
[suspenseful music playing]

622
00:36:26,476 --> 00:36:29,521
The camera's on you, which means
you were followed and they planned this.

623
00:36:29,605 --> 00:36:30,856
How did the hospital visit go?

624
00:36:30,939 --> 00:36:32,858
How do you know I'm in Bansang-dong?

625
00:36:34,192 --> 00:36:35,277
Will you marry me?

626
00:36:36,236 --> 00:36:39,448
Done. Still, just in case,
you should reset it before using it,

627
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:42,117
or take it to a service center.

628
00:36:45,078 --> 00:36:45,954
Ms. Kang?

629
00:36:46,538 --> 00:36:47,581
What?

630
00:36:48,332 --> 00:36:50,459
Um, what did you just say?

631
00:36:53,545 --> 00:36:56,131
My unit is 1601.

632
00:36:56,214 --> 00:36:57,758
Which floor are you?

633
00:36:59,134 --> 00:37:01,345
Huh? You're just one floor above me?

634
00:37:02,054 --> 00:37:03,722
[Sun-woo laughing]

635
00:37:07,017 --> 00:37:08,060
[clears throat]

636
00:37:13,690 --> 00:37:14,816
[elevator dings]

637
00:37:17,694 --> 00:37:19,863
You did great work today.
Have a good night.

638
00:37:19,947 --> 00:37:21,406
Uh... Yes, you too.

639
00:37:25,369 --> 00:37:27,162
[suspenseful music continues]

640
00:37:28,205 --> 00:37:29,831
HOW TO CHECK PHONE FOR HACKING APPS

641
00:37:36,296 --> 00:37:37,464
SIGNS OF POSSIBLE PHONE HACKING

642
00:37:37,547 --> 00:37:39,049
1. OVERHEATING
2. UNEXPLAINED STORAGE USAGE

643
00:37:40,842 --> 00:37:42,177
STORAGE - USING 89%
UNKNOWN FILES - 258.4 GB

644
00:37:44,012 --> 00:37:45,764
Wow, this place is big.

645
00:37:45,847 --> 00:37:47,182
-Yes.
-Is this my spot?

646
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:49,851
-Oh, yeah, I guess. So, is it okay?
-It's nice.

647
00:37:49,935 --> 00:37:50,769
What's with the tent?

648
00:37:50,852 --> 00:37:52,270
That belongs to my nephew.
It's Yun-seong's.

649
00:37:52,354 --> 00:37:54,523
-And your room?
-Oh, come here.

650
00:37:54,606 --> 00:37:55,482
It's amazing.

651
00:37:55,565 --> 00:37:58,360
-Ta-da!
-[Sun-woo] Wow, it is.

652
00:37:58,443 --> 00:37:59,403
Hey, it's nice.

653
00:37:59,486 --> 00:38:00,696
This is nice.

654
00:38:00,779 --> 00:38:03,448
Huh? Hey, let's stop looking now.
You might change your mind.

655
00:38:03,532 --> 00:38:05,033
So stop looking. Stop looking, you know.

656
00:38:05,117 --> 00:38:07,244
Was moving here a good idea or not?

657
00:38:07,327 --> 00:38:08,495
It was the best idea!

658
00:38:08,578 --> 00:38:11,748
Just listen to your big brother, Sun-woo.
We're going to make it big here, okay?

659
00:38:11,832 --> 00:38:13,000
Yeah, bro!

660
00:38:13,500 --> 00:38:15,460
[doorbell ringing]

661
00:38:17,629 --> 00:38:19,131
Ms. Kang?

662
00:38:19,214 --> 00:38:21,717
Hey, Sun-woo,
can you help me with something?

663
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,260
[Tae-jun sighs]

664
00:38:26,555 --> 00:38:28,390
[Tae-jun] There's a hidden app here.

665
00:38:30,267 --> 00:38:32,686
It's definitely
a location tracking program.

666
00:38:32,769 --> 00:38:35,772
This IP,
it's the same one who had the post.

667
00:38:35,856 --> 00:38:37,065
The hospital video.

668
00:38:37,149 --> 00:38:40,360
There's a record of the hacking app
sending location data there.

669
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:44,072
It says it's connected right now.
I think we can trace it back.

670
00:38:44,865 --> 00:38:46,283
[keyboard clacking]

671
00:38:49,953 --> 00:38:51,455
[beeping rapidly]

672
00:38:51,538 --> 00:38:54,666
SEOSEUNG HAEBIT APARTMENTS

673
00:38:54,750 --> 00:38:55,751
Got it.

674
00:38:58,712 --> 00:39:01,882
[sighs] There must be over 300 apartments
in that complex.

675
00:39:01,965 --> 00:39:03,884
I think I might know where it is.

676
00:39:07,387 --> 00:39:08,638
SALES TEAM MANAGER KIM DONG-SEOK

677
00:39:08,722 --> 00:39:09,598
[cell phone vibrating]

678
00:39:09,681 --> 00:39:10,557
MY GIRLFRIEND

679
00:39:10,640 --> 00:39:13,518
Must be busy.
She'll come over when she sees the call.

680
00:39:13,602 --> 00:39:16,021
-Let's drink together for now.
-Good job today.

681
00:39:18,190 --> 00:39:20,525
[all grunting]

682
00:39:21,943 --> 00:39:25,280
Oh! Ms. Kang! Oh, you really came.

683
00:39:25,363 --> 00:39:26,740
[chuckles]

684
00:39:26,823 --> 00:39:27,991
Yi-ji...

685
00:39:28,075 --> 00:39:29,576
[stammers] Weren't you busy?

686
00:39:29,659 --> 00:39:31,912
-Please sit here.
-Yes, Yi-ji, take a seat.

687
00:39:32,913 --> 00:39:34,581
Do you want to talk here?

688
00:39:38,752 --> 00:39:40,378
[man 1] Hey, can we get
another one of those?

689
00:39:40,462 --> 00:39:41,463
[man 2] Yeah.

690
00:39:42,839 --> 00:39:44,508
You didn't answer my call,
but you still came.

691
00:39:45,634 --> 00:39:47,552
This ID was secretly trying to install

692
00:39:47,636 --> 00:39:49,096
a location tracking app
on his wife's phone.

693
00:39:49,179 --> 00:39:50,806
KMH91.

694
00:39:50,889 --> 00:39:53,308
Kim Myeong-hun.
Your real name before you changed it.

695
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:55,685
These are the initials, right?

696
00:39:55,769 --> 00:39:56,853
[Dong-seok chuckles]

697
00:39:56,937 --> 00:39:59,064
I really don't know how to explain this.

698
00:39:59,147 --> 00:40:01,066
A friend of mine suspects
his wife of something.

699
00:40:01,149 --> 00:40:04,152
-So a few days ago, using my ID--
-This was posted a month ago.

700
00:40:05,987 --> 00:40:07,114
Uh, that, uh...

701
00:40:07,906 --> 00:40:10,450
You installed a location tracking app
on my phone, too.

702
00:40:10,534 --> 00:40:12,160
When did you take my phone?

703
00:40:12,244 --> 00:40:13,120
It's not me.

704
00:40:13,203 --> 00:40:17,124
[scoffs] You followed me
and maliciously posted that video.

705
00:40:17,207 --> 00:40:18,416
Why did you go that far?

706
00:40:19,334 --> 00:40:21,336
[suspenseful music playing]

707
00:40:23,004 --> 00:40:26,133
I hated that you were
so obsessed with work.

708
00:40:26,633 --> 00:40:28,969
So then you wanted
to make me quit the company?

709
00:40:29,052 --> 00:40:32,848
Someone like Mr. Song will never
acknowledge you unless you bow down.

710
00:40:32,931 --> 00:40:35,308
Why are you hanging on
so stubbornly to those people?

711
00:40:35,392 --> 00:40:39,396
No, it isn't that you hate me
refusing to bow down to Mr. Song.

712
00:40:39,479 --> 00:40:42,107
If I wouldn't even bow down
to someone like him,

713
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:45,277
you know very well there was no way
I'd bow down to someone like you.

714
00:40:45,360 --> 00:40:46,695
Isn't that it?

715
00:40:50,740 --> 00:40:51,992
What?

716
00:40:53,451 --> 00:40:55,078
-You're that--
-Forget it.

717
00:40:55,162 --> 00:40:58,248
We'll continue this at the police station.

718
00:40:58,832 --> 00:41:00,834
[Ji-won] I knew it. I knew it!

719
00:41:00,917 --> 00:41:03,420
Something felt off.
I knew something was up with you.

720
00:41:03,503 --> 00:41:06,381
What kind of a scumbag does that?
You should punish him.

721
00:41:07,757 --> 00:41:09,384
I've already been to the police.

722
00:41:10,051 --> 00:41:11,595
You have? [clicks tongue]

723
00:41:12,220 --> 00:41:16,141
You know, you really can't
judge a person by appearances.

724
00:41:16,224 --> 00:41:17,642
No. You know, we can.

725
00:41:17,726 --> 00:41:19,060
Remember when he was proposing?

726
00:41:19,144 --> 00:41:22,272
That idiot was mostly
filming his own face. [scoffs]

727
00:41:22,898 --> 00:41:24,107
And what about your mom?

728
00:41:24,191 --> 00:41:26,067
What does she say?
I mean, she really liked him.

729
00:41:26,693 --> 00:41:28,278
I don't have the heart to tell her.

730
00:41:28,361 --> 00:41:32,032
You know her health hasn't been good
since she collapsed last time.

731
00:41:32,115 --> 00:41:33,158
That's true.

732
00:41:33,241 --> 00:41:36,286
And with her temper,
if she found out, he'd be half-dead.

733
00:41:36,369 --> 00:41:38,705
You know, he's a really lucky guy
if you think about it.

734
00:41:38,788 --> 00:41:40,081
[Yi-ji chuckles]

735
00:41:41,374 --> 00:41:43,585
But is it okay for you
to be here this late?

736
00:41:43,668 --> 00:41:45,378
[chuckles] Oh, of course.

737
00:41:45,462 --> 00:41:47,631
I should be by your side
on a day like this.

738
00:41:48,715 --> 00:41:50,508
You have been through so much.

739
00:41:51,092 --> 00:41:52,928
I'm fine. So go ahead and get home.

740
00:41:53,553 --> 00:41:55,388
No, don't worry about it.

741
00:41:55,472 --> 00:41:58,141
I'll tell Yong-woon
to stop by on his way home.

742
00:41:58,225 --> 00:42:00,185
Tomorrow, he's finally got a day off.

743
00:42:00,268 --> 00:42:02,020
You'll finally get to go on a date.

744
00:42:02,103 --> 00:42:04,356
But that's that, and today's today.

745
00:42:05,065 --> 00:42:07,317
Yi-ji, let's just drink.

746
00:42:09,236 --> 00:42:10,278
Cheers.

747
00:42:23,708 --> 00:42:25,335
[Yong-woon laughing]

748
00:42:25,418 --> 00:42:26,878
[Yong-woon's mother laughing]

749
00:42:26,962 --> 00:42:28,546
Goodness. [laughs]

750
00:42:29,464 --> 00:42:33,426
Having a child in the house
makes the mood so bright, don't you think?

751
00:42:33,510 --> 00:42:34,719
What about you two?

752
00:42:34,803 --> 00:42:38,515
[sighs] If it's because you're feeling
lonely, see Yu-jun more often.

753
00:42:38,598 --> 00:42:40,934
But he has a different surname.

754
00:42:41,017 --> 00:42:44,479
You two, are you choosing
not to have children, or can't you?

755
00:42:44,562 --> 00:42:46,106
[Yong-woon sighs]

756
00:42:46,189 --> 00:42:48,358
We really just don't want to have any.

757
00:42:48,900 --> 00:42:50,068
[cell phone vibrating]

758
00:42:50,151 --> 00:42:51,444
Just one moment.

759
00:42:52,404 --> 00:42:53,905
[Yong-woon's mother]
I really need an answer.

760
00:42:53,989 --> 00:42:56,074
Are you sure
you're not going to have a child?

761
00:42:56,157 --> 00:42:58,410
Oh, Yong-woon is too busy.

762
00:42:58,493 --> 00:43:00,996
Goodness. Are you going
to keep making up excuses?

763
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:03,873
And you, stop referring
to him so casually.

764
00:43:03,957 --> 00:43:05,792
You've been married long enough.

765
00:43:05,875 --> 00:43:08,295
-[Ji-won chuckles]
-[Yong-woon's mother sighs]

766
00:43:08,378 --> 00:43:10,463
At first, I thought
you two were just saying that.

767
00:43:11,464 --> 00:43:15,093
What will you do if you want a child
when you're older and it's too late?

768
00:43:15,176 --> 00:43:17,137
Some things you just can't delay.

769
00:43:17,220 --> 00:43:19,222
[Un-jeong]
Oh, Mom, please don't say those things.

770
00:43:20,473 --> 00:43:23,101
Plenty of couples
are perfectly happy without children.

771
00:43:23,184 --> 00:43:24,519
[Yong-woon's mother]
Early in your marriage,

772
00:43:24,602 --> 00:43:26,104
when you went traveling alone,

773
00:43:26,187 --> 00:43:29,232
I honestly thought
you two would end up splitting up.

774
00:43:29,899 --> 00:43:32,360
[sighs] You're home
all the time these days.

775
00:43:32,444 --> 00:43:34,612
And the opportunity is just right.

776
00:43:35,363 --> 00:43:37,699
[Yong-woon] Mom, it's a holiday.

777
00:43:38,283 --> 00:43:39,993
Would you like to go out for dinner?

778
00:43:40,785 --> 00:43:42,495
[sighs in exasperation] Forget it.

779
00:43:54,174 --> 00:43:57,344
[sighs] Why would your mother
say something like that?

780
00:43:57,427 --> 00:43:59,679
She probably said that
because she wants a grandchild.

781
00:43:59,763 --> 00:44:02,015
Your parents in Yangjae-dong
say the exact same thing.

782
00:44:02,932 --> 00:44:04,059
-Yong-woon.
-Mm?

783
00:44:04,726 --> 00:44:06,311
[sighs deeply]

784
00:44:06,394 --> 00:44:07,854
I mean, sweetie.

785
00:44:09,272 --> 00:44:10,273
Just tell me.

786
00:44:11,399 --> 00:44:13,985
Did your mother want us to...

787
00:44:15,445 --> 00:44:16,988
divorce when we got married?

788
00:44:18,114 --> 00:44:19,532
Why bring up the past again?

789
00:44:20,950 --> 00:44:22,535
She says you're doing well now.

790
00:44:22,619 --> 00:44:25,413
I'm asking if she wanted us to divorce.

791
00:44:25,497 --> 00:44:27,957
[sighs deeply] I...

792
00:44:29,292 --> 00:44:32,212
really like seeing you take an interest
in homemaking these days.

793
00:44:32,295 --> 00:44:33,505
Makes me glad

794
00:44:34,172 --> 00:44:36,132
that I waited for you.

795
00:44:36,216 --> 00:44:39,427
And we finally feel
like a normal family now.

796
00:44:39,511 --> 00:44:40,678
Hmm?

797
00:44:41,471 --> 00:44:43,973
Yong-woon, so we were
abnormal before that?

798
00:44:45,058 --> 00:44:46,935
You're the one who said it.

799
00:44:47,018 --> 00:44:48,853
You said that all you needed was me.

800
00:44:48,937 --> 00:44:50,980
That just the two of us
would be enough to be happy.

801
00:44:51,064 --> 00:44:53,316
Some things can change over time.

802
00:44:54,067 --> 00:44:56,027
[pensive music playing]

803
00:44:56,111 --> 00:44:57,070
[inhales sharply]

804
00:44:57,153 --> 00:45:00,740
So our decision not to have any kids,
that hasn't changed, right?

805
00:45:03,535 --> 00:45:08,373
Actually, I do want a child,
at least right now.

806
00:45:08,456 --> 00:45:09,833
What?

807
00:45:09,916 --> 00:45:11,668
But if you don't want one,

808
00:45:11,751 --> 00:45:13,962
I can protect you
from my mother's nagging.

809
00:45:14,045 --> 00:45:15,672
[sighs softly]

810
00:45:20,969 --> 00:45:24,556
You know, I didn't want to bring it up
because I might look petty here,

811
00:45:25,932 --> 00:45:28,143
but you didn't even celebrate my birthday.

812
00:45:28,226 --> 00:45:30,770
And today was your one day off
in two weeks,

813
00:45:30,854 --> 00:45:33,523
and we spend one of those days
at your parents' house.

814
00:45:33,606 --> 00:45:36,651
And now you bring up... having a child?

815
00:45:36,734 --> 00:45:42,323
I'm real sorry, but I'm not saying
we should have one right now.

816
00:45:42,407 --> 00:45:43,741
I'm okay with waiting.

817
00:45:43,825 --> 00:45:47,328
You call it waiting, but in the end,
you're telling me to have a kid.

818
00:45:47,412 --> 00:45:48,621
All right.

819
00:45:49,664 --> 00:45:50,874
If you don't want to,

820
00:45:52,125 --> 00:45:54,794
[sighs] let's not have one...
for right now.

821
00:45:55,879 --> 00:45:57,464
[sighs deeply]

822
00:46:10,101 --> 00:46:11,269
[turnstile beeping]

823
00:46:17,901 --> 00:46:20,653
Thank you for not telling the company.

824
00:46:21,237 --> 00:46:22,864
I applied for a transfer.

825
00:46:24,032 --> 00:46:27,535
I'm not saying I want to get back
together now or anything.

826
00:46:28,161 --> 00:46:29,787
I ruined it and it's over.

827
00:46:30,371 --> 00:46:31,456
Just, uh,

828
00:46:32,624 --> 00:46:34,292
please don't despise me too much.

829
00:46:34,375 --> 00:46:36,044
[quirky music playing]

830
00:46:36,127 --> 00:46:38,046
Did you forget the restraining order?

831
00:46:38,129 --> 00:46:40,006
Make sure we don't ever talk again.

832
00:46:45,929 --> 00:46:47,138
-Ah, yes.
-[woman] Hello.

833
00:46:47,222 --> 00:46:48,181
Yes. Hello. Yes.

834
00:46:48,264 --> 00:46:50,141
[quirky music builds]

835
00:47:01,444 --> 00:47:02,779
[Dong-seok exclaims]

836
00:47:03,988 --> 00:47:05,823
-[man] Are you all right?
-[stammers]

837
00:47:05,907 --> 00:47:08,785
Yes, I'm fine.
You don't have to pick them up for me.

838
00:47:08,868 --> 00:47:11,120
Uh, yes, yes. I got it. Thank you.

839
00:47:11,204 --> 00:47:13,248
[suspenseful music playing]

840
00:47:15,917 --> 00:47:17,877
-Ms. Kang?
-What is it, ma'am?

841
00:47:17,961 --> 00:47:21,631
Put in a little more work and finish
sorting the promotional materials.

842
00:47:23,049 --> 00:47:24,300
Ah!

843
00:47:24,384 --> 00:47:27,720
I heard you broke up
with Manager Kim Dong-seok from Sales?

844
00:47:29,347 --> 00:47:31,975
Oh... I'm worried about you

845
00:47:32,058 --> 00:47:33,726
-in all sorts of ways these days.
-What's wrong with her?

846
00:47:33,810 --> 00:47:36,521
Have I given you too much work
during a difficult time?

847
00:47:37,397 --> 00:47:38,815
Oh, no, I'm just fine.

848
00:47:38,898 --> 00:47:39,941
You're fine?

849
00:47:40,024 --> 00:47:42,527
[gasps] Then you've already found
another boyfriend?

850
00:47:42,610 --> 00:47:44,153
Not yet, ma'am.

851
00:47:44,237 --> 00:47:45,321
No?

852
00:47:46,906 --> 00:47:49,367
Then did Mr. Kim find another woman?

853
00:47:49,951 --> 00:47:51,536
[gasps] Did he cheat on you?

854
00:47:53,246 --> 00:47:54,664
I mean...

855
00:47:55,415 --> 00:47:56,874
everyone's curious,

856
00:47:56,958 --> 00:47:58,668
and I'm not one to talk
behind people's back.

857
00:47:58,751 --> 00:47:59,836
All right.

858
00:47:59,919 --> 00:48:02,922
We'll call it personal differences,
and it ended on good terms.

859
00:48:03,006 --> 00:48:04,507
Oh. Hang in there.

860
00:48:05,425 --> 00:48:07,844
Oh, it's such a shame.
He was so right for you.

861
00:48:07,927 --> 00:48:08,928
-Ms. Lee...
-Yes?

862
00:48:13,349 --> 00:48:15,393
I haven't found another man,

863
00:48:15,476 --> 00:48:17,895
and Mr. Kim hasn't found
another woman either.

864
00:48:18,688 --> 00:48:21,024
I thought I should just
make those facts clear.

865
00:48:21,107 --> 00:48:24,444
Oh! This is the problem
with office romances.

866
00:48:24,527 --> 00:48:27,864
In the end, Mr. Kim had to go
to the Gangwon branch because of you.

867
00:48:27,947 --> 00:48:30,366
His performance may have been lacking,
but he was such a nice guy.

868
00:48:30,450 --> 00:48:31,868
That's not it.

869
00:48:31,951 --> 00:48:34,495
As I understand it,
it wasn't a management decision.

870
00:48:34,579 --> 00:48:36,122
He volunteered to go.

871
00:48:36,205 --> 00:48:38,750
Really? That's not exactly what I heard.

872
00:48:41,044 --> 00:48:42,295
Look, Ms. Lee...

873
00:48:43,296 --> 00:48:45,840
I'd appreciate it
if you stopped discussing

874
00:48:45,923 --> 00:48:47,800
my private matters during work hours.

875
00:48:47,884 --> 00:48:50,762
Why? I'm only saying that
to get closer to you.

876
00:48:50,845 --> 00:48:54,390
Goodness, you can't say anything
to young people these days.

877
00:48:54,474 --> 00:48:58,019
[laughs] But actually, you aren't
even really that young, are you?

878
00:48:58,102 --> 00:49:01,689
Discussing an employee's private life
openly like this during work hours

879
00:49:01,773 --> 00:49:04,275
can be seen
as a violation of their rights,

880
00:49:05,026 --> 00:49:07,195
and it interferes with their work.

881
00:49:09,572 --> 00:49:12,617
You certainly have
an answer for everything.

882
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:15,244
If necessary,
I can formally raise the issue

883
00:49:15,328 --> 00:49:17,497
with the Audit Team at headquarters.

884
00:49:18,581 --> 00:49:21,376
What? The Audit Team?

885
00:49:21,459 --> 00:49:22,377
[papers rustling]

886
00:49:23,586 --> 00:49:25,171
Ms. Kang, please take a look at this.

887
00:49:27,507 --> 00:49:30,301
[gasps dramatically, laughs]

888
00:49:30,385 --> 00:49:31,427
Did you hear that?

889
00:49:31,511 --> 00:49:33,554
The Audit Team. [laughs]

890
00:49:33,638 --> 00:49:37,058
She said "Audit Team."
Oh, she's something else.

891
00:49:37,141 --> 00:49:39,018
[Jung-eun sighs dramatically]

892
00:49:44,482 --> 00:49:46,150
[Yi-ji sighs]

893
00:49:46,234 --> 00:49:47,694
[keyboard clacking]

894
00:49:50,863 --> 00:49:52,990
[Ki-tae] Hey, Ms. Kang. [chuckles]

895
00:49:53,866 --> 00:49:56,661
Are you all right working
within the Management Support Team?

896
00:49:56,744 --> 00:49:57,704
Yes.

897
00:49:58,788 --> 00:50:00,873
May I at least carry that for you?

898
00:50:00,957 --> 00:50:02,542
I think I can manage.

899
00:50:02,625 --> 00:50:04,419
[sighs] You know what?

900
00:50:06,170 --> 00:50:08,423
I do respect you. I mean it.

901
00:50:08,506 --> 00:50:10,508
If it were me, I would have run away.

902
00:50:10,591 --> 00:50:12,885
They say you should leave
while they're still applauding.

903
00:50:12,969 --> 00:50:17,098
You could have made a glamorous exit
wearing a wedding dress, right?

904
00:50:17,181 --> 00:50:18,599
The news must have made the rounds by now.

905
00:50:18,683 --> 00:50:20,435
-You're slow with gossip.
-Why?

906
00:50:21,144 --> 00:50:23,020
Is there something else I don't know?

907
00:50:23,104 --> 00:50:24,480
[Yi-ji scoffs]

908
00:50:24,564 --> 00:50:27,400
Who gets a glamorous exit
in this day and age?

909
00:50:27,483 --> 00:50:29,402
Isn't your thinking a little outdated?

910
00:50:29,485 --> 00:50:31,821
Since you insisted on carrying this,

911
00:50:31,904 --> 00:50:33,531
I'll ask you to take it
as far as the storeroom.

912
00:50:33,614 --> 00:50:36,033
Oh, sure. I can do that.

913
00:50:36,701 --> 00:50:37,827
[grunts]

914
00:50:39,954 --> 00:50:41,914
Aah! Acting all tough.

915
00:50:43,499 --> 00:50:46,210
Oh! Why is this so heavy?

916
00:50:46,836 --> 00:50:48,713
She really is tough. Geez.

917
00:50:51,591 --> 00:50:53,009
Well, Mr. Han Sun-woo.

918
00:50:53,092 --> 00:50:54,719
Is the work going well?

919
00:50:54,802 --> 00:50:57,680
Promotional materials aren't finished,
but I did the magazines.

920
00:50:57,764 --> 00:50:59,557
Oh, you two work well together.

921
00:50:59,640 --> 00:51:02,435
-Have you worked together very long?
-No, it hasn't been long.

922
00:51:02,518 --> 00:51:04,854
Really? What a shame.

923
00:51:04,937 --> 00:51:08,483
You didn't have to follow her
out of Legal Affairs. Why did you?

924
00:51:08,566 --> 00:51:10,276
Was someone bullying you?

925
00:51:10,359 --> 00:51:14,781
No, ma'am. I wanted to learn how to do
a proper job under a capable boss.

926
00:51:14,864 --> 00:51:17,325
In the Management Support Team? From whom?

927
00:51:18,367 --> 00:51:20,870
[laughs]

928
00:51:20,953 --> 00:51:23,122
Oh, seriously! From me?

929
00:51:23,206 --> 00:51:24,791
[both laughing]

930
00:51:24,874 --> 00:51:25,958
From Senior Manager Kang.

931
00:51:26,042 --> 00:51:27,460
-[stops laughing]
-[staff tittering]

932
00:51:27,543 --> 00:51:29,170
Work that would take anyone else a week

933
00:51:29,253 --> 00:51:31,506
is finished in two days
when she takes it on.

934
00:51:32,048 --> 00:51:33,966
[chuckles] Oh, really?

935
00:51:34,050 --> 00:51:35,218
Then finish up the job.

936
00:51:35,301 --> 00:51:36,677
Yeah.

937
00:51:50,650 --> 00:51:52,652
[gentle music playing]

938
00:52:03,538 --> 00:52:04,789
I'll get it.

939
00:52:05,665 --> 00:52:06,833
[Sun-woo grunts]

940
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:10,920
I heard what you said
to Ms. Lee earlier today.

941
00:52:11,587 --> 00:52:12,630
Why did you do that?

942
00:52:12,713 --> 00:52:16,843
She's above me in rank and could influence
whether you become a permanent employee.

943
00:52:17,552 --> 00:52:20,847
She keeps picking on you.
How do you manage to stay so calm?

944
00:52:20,930 --> 00:52:24,725
I don't pay mind to what people say
when they don't really know me.

945
00:52:24,809 --> 00:52:26,727
Even if I do, it won't change the job.

946
00:52:26,811 --> 00:52:28,771
As long as it doesn't
interfere with my work.

947
00:52:28,855 --> 00:52:30,022
But sometimes that messes you up.

948
00:52:30,106 --> 00:52:32,191
I mean, you got transferred
to another department.

949
00:52:33,568 --> 00:52:34,861
I rarely regret things.

950
00:52:34,944 --> 00:52:37,905
At every moment, I made
my own judgments and choices.

951
00:52:38,656 --> 00:52:42,076
And if I can learn something new here now,
that's enough for me.

952
00:52:46,289 --> 00:52:47,748
[gentle music fades]

953
00:52:47,832 --> 00:52:50,793
We're about 78% done
distributing the guidelines.

954
00:52:50,877 --> 00:52:52,879
The switch to wired connections
is complete,

955
00:52:52,962 --> 00:52:54,171
and regional adjustments are underway.

956
00:52:54,797 --> 00:52:56,132
[Jung-eun] Hmm.

957
00:52:56,215 --> 00:52:58,926
-Check the service centers carefully, too.
-Yes, ma'am.

958
00:52:59,010 --> 00:53:00,219
Oh, Ms. Kang?

959
00:53:00,303 --> 00:53:01,137
Yes, Ms. Lee?

960
00:53:01,220 --> 00:53:03,472
Could you sort the brand
promotional materials

961
00:53:03,556 --> 00:53:05,933
in the storeroom by month
and bring them to me?

962
00:53:06,017 --> 00:53:07,059
-Right now?
-Yes.

963
00:53:07,143 --> 00:53:08,978
I need it for the meeting.

964
00:53:09,061 --> 00:53:12,523
You've spent a few days in the storeroom,
so you must know it by now. Would you?

965
00:53:13,107 --> 00:53:14,567
-Yes.
-Right.

966
00:53:17,987 --> 00:53:21,073
Mr. Han, why are you sitting there?
Shouldn't you go with her?

967
00:53:21,699 --> 00:53:22,909
Yeah.

968
00:53:22,992 --> 00:53:24,702
[Jung-eun] Got it?

969
00:53:24,785 --> 00:53:26,495
Don't upset the people at headquarters.

970
00:53:27,580 --> 00:53:28,831
Yes. Good work.

971
00:53:32,084 --> 00:53:33,085
You can go.

972
00:53:36,631 --> 00:53:37,465
Oh.

973
00:53:38,090 --> 00:53:41,344
This project started before you came,
so you don't need to attend.

974
00:53:41,427 --> 00:53:44,889
I'd like you to go finish
organizing the storeroom.

975
00:53:45,514 --> 00:53:47,516
[intriguing music playing]

976
00:54:11,207 --> 00:54:12,625
Ahh!

977
00:54:12,708 --> 00:54:14,460
Going that far.

978
00:54:14,543 --> 00:54:15,962
She really is persistent.

979
00:54:17,171 --> 00:54:18,255
[Ki-tae sighs]

980
00:54:21,175 --> 00:54:22,969
[intriguing music fades]

981
00:54:28,975 --> 00:54:30,226
Oh!

982
00:54:30,309 --> 00:54:31,852
"General Manager Jung Ki-tae."

983
00:54:31,936 --> 00:54:33,479
His nameplate has arrived.

984
00:54:33,562 --> 00:54:35,564
"Congratulations on being promoted."

985
00:54:35,648 --> 00:54:37,066
Who will take it to him?

986
00:54:39,735 --> 00:54:42,071
Who will go to Legal Affairs?

987
00:54:45,574 --> 00:54:47,201
I'll go and take it.

988
00:54:47,994 --> 00:54:50,079
[pensive music playing]

989
00:54:50,162 --> 00:54:51,205
You will?

990
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:52,665
Will you be all right?

991
00:54:53,207 --> 00:54:54,208
Yes.

992
00:54:55,501 --> 00:54:56,627
Okay, then.

993
00:54:57,503 --> 00:54:59,380
Take this potted plant as well.

994
00:55:04,760 --> 00:55:08,055
At work, working hard
doesn't always mean you win.

995
00:55:08,639 --> 00:55:11,976
People who have done things the right way
don't always get the recognition for it.

996
00:55:13,602 --> 00:55:17,356
Relationships over ability,
power over results.

997
00:55:17,440 --> 00:55:20,067
It always mixes up everything, every time.

998
00:55:20,651 --> 00:55:22,236
I know, because I've been through it.

999
00:55:22,319 --> 00:55:23,946
[inspiring music playing]

1000
00:55:24,905 --> 00:55:26,949
[Byung-je] You should
just make a graceful exit instead.

1001
00:55:27,033 --> 00:55:29,076
It's impressive you've lasted this long.

1002
00:55:29,160 --> 00:55:32,872
[Ki-tae] I really respect you.
If it were me, I would have run away.

1003
00:55:32,955 --> 00:55:35,583
[Dong-seok] Why are you hanging on
so stubbornly to those people?

1004
00:55:36,584 --> 00:55:40,296
[Yi-ji] Maybe that's why
every time I fall,

1005
00:55:40,379 --> 00:55:43,049
I think my center actually grows stronger.

1006
00:55:50,347 --> 00:55:53,059
I'm not someone who breaks
when people try to crush me.

1007
00:55:55,811 --> 00:55:59,190
I'm someone who
holds on to the end and shows them.

1008
00:56:03,235 --> 00:56:06,280
EPILOGUE

1009
00:56:06,363 --> 00:56:07,323
[Ji-won] But Yi-ji,

1010
00:56:07,406 --> 00:56:10,951
do you know what happens
when you really fall in love?

1011
00:56:14,205 --> 00:56:17,041
Still, it's so bright
with the moon out, isn't it?

1012
00:56:17,124 --> 00:56:18,626
[romantic music playing]

1013
00:56:18,709 --> 00:56:20,169
[Ji-won] When you're in love,

1014
00:56:22,213 --> 00:56:24,924
all you can think about is that person.

1015
00:56:25,007 --> 00:56:27,927
Your head is filled
entirely with that person.

1016
00:56:28,761 --> 00:56:30,387
[Tae-jun] Yo, bro, I'm home.

1017
00:56:31,097 --> 00:56:32,932
Oh. You came back early.

1018
00:56:33,015 --> 00:56:34,350
Eun-ha, just wait a second.

1019
00:56:36,560 --> 00:56:38,020
Eun-ha, put these on.

1020
00:56:38,562 --> 00:56:40,564
-The floor is dirty.
-[Eun-ha] Thank you.

1021
00:56:40,648 --> 00:56:42,775
[Ji-won] You show
behaviors and expressions

1022
00:56:42,858 --> 00:56:45,528
that are totally different
from the way you usually are.

1023
00:56:45,611 --> 00:56:47,321
[sighs] Remember that time?

1024
00:56:47,404 --> 00:56:51,325
Tae-jun's last three-point
at the winter basketball tournament.

1025
00:56:51,408 --> 00:56:53,160
[chuckles] That was so long ago.

1026
00:56:54,036 --> 00:56:55,788
Mm. You even had a fan club back then.

1027
00:56:55,871 --> 00:56:57,039
You were a star player.

1028
00:56:57,123 --> 00:56:59,375
You looked really cool
when you played basketball.

1029
00:56:59,458 --> 00:57:01,502
-You still play?
-I do sometimes with Sun-woo.

1030
00:57:01,585 --> 00:57:04,171
I want to come watch.
I wanna see you guys play.

1031
00:57:04,922 --> 00:57:06,257
-Okay.
-[chuckles] Cheers!

1032
00:57:06,340 --> 00:57:07,591
Cheers.

1033
00:57:07,675 --> 00:57:09,218
[Eun-ha laughs]

1034
00:57:09,301 --> 00:57:11,554
[Ji-won]
Then when you think about reality,

1035
00:57:11,637 --> 00:57:13,556
you get scared for no reason.

1036
00:57:13,639 --> 00:57:15,516
You lose your confidence.

1037
00:57:15,599 --> 00:57:18,352
[romantic music continues]

1038
00:57:18,435 --> 00:57:19,854
But even so, love...

1039
00:57:20,771 --> 00:57:23,357
makes your heart flutter
like spring flowers.

1040
00:57:23,440 --> 00:57:25,901
And then it burns out like the summer sun.

1041
00:57:27,444 --> 00:57:30,447
It takes on these beautiful colors
like autumn leaves.

1042
00:57:32,074 --> 00:57:35,911
And you find yourself waiting for it
like the first snow of winter.

1043
00:57:36,537 --> 00:57:39,498
Anyway, it's something wonderful.

1044
00:57:39,582 --> 00:57:41,417
It's just so wonderful.

1045
00:57:41,500 --> 00:57:44,545
♪ We're writing our own story ♪

1046
00:57:44,628 --> 00:57:47,548
♪ We don't ever have to be alone ♪

1047
00:57:49,675 --> 00:57:54,180
♪ Oh, I've been feeling low ♪

1048
00:57:54,263 --> 00:57:59,143
♪ Till you showed up at my door ♪

1049
00:57:59,226 --> 00:58:01,270
♪ Just want to prove to you ♪

1050
00:58:01,353 --> 00:58:04,398
♪ I'll be there to give my all ♪

1051
00:58:04,481 --> 00:58:08,027
♪ I'll answer to every call ♪

1052
00:58:08,110 --> 00:58:10,863
♪ You and I, it's all or nothing ♪

1053
00:58:10,946 --> 00:58:12,531
♪ 'Cause, girl, you are ♪

1054
00:58:12,615 --> 00:58:15,534
♪ The one that could make me smile ♪

1055
00:58:15,618 --> 00:58:18,537
♪ I'm running a thousand miles ♪

1056
00:58:18,621 --> 00:58:21,540
♪ Loving you is not like ♪

1057
00:58:21,624 --> 00:58:24,543
♪ Loving me, oh, no ♪

1058
00:58:25,794 --> 00:58:27,546
♪ It could be getting late ♪

1059
00:58:28,756 --> 00:58:30,549
♪ But would like to stay ♪

1060
00:58:31,592 --> 00:58:33,552
♪ Baby, yeah, won't you say? ♪

1061
00:58:33,636 --> 00:58:35,679
♪ Just want to prove to you ♪

1062
00:58:35,763 --> 00:58:38,515
♪ I'll be there to give my all ♪

1063
00:58:39,642 --> 00:58:41,977
It's true. Ms. Kang
is a little demanding, yeah.

1064
00:58:42,478 --> 00:58:44,063
[Yi-ji] I'll say this just once.

1065
00:58:44,146 --> 00:58:45,981
The moment you followed me
out of Legal Affairs,

1066
00:58:46,065 --> 00:58:47,900
I considered you as one of my people.

1067
00:58:48,734 --> 00:58:49,735
What do you think you're doing now?

1068
00:58:49,818 --> 00:58:51,237
[Yi-ji] I'm making a bomb.

1069
00:58:51,320 --> 00:58:52,196
Nice!

1070
00:58:52,279 --> 00:58:54,823
[Ki-tae] I hear he's someone
headquarters trusts a great deal.

1071
00:58:54,907 --> 00:58:58,077
[Jung-eun] It was my understanding
you agreed to the overtime work.

1072
00:58:58,160 --> 00:58:59,495
[Sun-woo]
Looks like we're working late again.

1073
00:58:59,578 --> 00:59:01,538
Could you spare me some time today?

1074
00:59:01,622 --> 00:59:05,251
[Yi-ji] Romance is just a trick
our hormones play on us.

1075
00:59:05,334 --> 00:59:08,879
[Sun-woo] You're one of the few people
I truly admire, Ms. Kang.

1076
00:59:10,714 --> 00:59:12,591
[romantic music fades]
